// SupplyCurrent: the front end's current per rail (README.md, "Supply current"). Every
// amplifier draws its typical quiescent current (parts/analog_*: ADA4817 19 mA, AD8130
// 10.8 mA, ADA4807 1.0 mA on +/-4.5 V and 0.915 mA on 3.3 V) plus the current its output
// delivers, from the rail that sources it; the rails are FrontEndPorts' ideal supplies,
// so I(POS) is the current the TPS7A4901 would deliver.
//  - idle: the operating point with the DDS at its DC level (0 V), as DcOperatingPoint;
//  - driving: the DDS at 1 MHz, where the guard drivers and sense buffers charge their
//    strays hardest, at its nominal 0.3 V peak and at 0.65 V (the top of the AD9833's
//    range), into dry soil (1.3 kohm m: R_TRANSFER 11 kohm, the largest pump swing) and
//    into moist loam (100 ohm m: 800 ohm); the rail currents averaged over ten periods
//    after the drive has settled (20 us to 30 us, as in Distortion).
// The hand estimate (README.md) is 51.8 mA per +/-4.5 V rail and 3.7 mA on V3V3_ANA
// typical, with signal currents "under 2 mA". The rails are sized for 70 mA per rail
// (board.copper: the TPS65130 inductor currents, and VPOS_F / VNEG_F declared at a 70 mA
// drop across the 1 ohm post-filters): that is the limit.
bench SupplyCurrent for AnalogFrontEnd using FrontEndPorts, SoilModel {
    param A_DDS = 0.3V;
    param HAND_ESTIMATE = 51.8mA;
    model DDS: source {
        out = DDS_OUT; ref = GND; ac = 0.3V; output_resistance = 200ohm;
        waveform = sine { amplitude = A_DDS; frequency = 1MHz; };
    }
    step R_TRANSFER, A_DDS in (11kohm, 0.3V), (11kohm, 0.65V), (800ohm, 0.3V);

    analysis idle: op;
    measure positive_rail = I(POS) { max = 70mA; }
    measure negative_rail = -I(NEG) { max = 70mA; }
    measure analog_3v3 = I(ANALOG_3V3);
    measure mid_reference = I(MID);
    measure positive_against_hand = I(POS) - HAND_ESTIMATE;

    analysis driving: tran { stop = 30us; start = 20us; max_step = 5ns; }
    measure positive_mean = mean(I(POS)) { max = 70mA; }
    measure negative_mean = -mean(I(NEG)) { max = 70mA; }
    measure positive_signal = mean(I(POS)) - HAND_ESTIMATE;
    measure negative_signal = -mean(I(NEG)) - HAND_ESTIMATE;
    measure positive_peak = max(I(POS));
    measure negative_peak = -min(I(NEG));
    measure analog_3v3_mean = mean(I(ANALOG_3V3));
    plot I(POS), I(NEG), I(ANALOG_3V3);
}
